{
	title: 'READ batches retain durable images on every surface',
	spec: 'READ accepts multiple local paths and URLs in mixed text/image batches. Every successful image remains attached even when another path fails; complete failure messages and the tool error flag survive. Validate and durably store every image through existing session blobs, preserving per-image caps, text UTF-8/binary checks, range behavior and editing versions. Existing single-image histories remain readable. All provider replay mappings, pruning estimates and recovery, READ_BLOB, transcript and terminal/web image consumers handle multiple images; native tool count and model-facing schema stay unchanged. READ_BLOB of a history record recovers every image across sibling tool results, legacy image fields, image arrays and direct image blocks while preserving the existing complete paged text. Missing or unreadable image blobs preserve all available siblings and return complete source-labeled errors with the tool error flag, including when none remain. HELP describes batches without an images-alone workaround. Focused regression tests cover multiple images after source deletion, mixed failures, persistence/replay across providers, shared UI image items and partial or total image recovery failures.',
