		'Invariant restored: batched READ must keep every successful image despite sibling failures. The old batch stringified image labels and threw the combined failure, which discarded attachments. Additive images plus the legacy image field keep old histories and single-image outputs readable. tools.run validates/stores each image exactly once; an internal source label identifies storage/validation failures. Replay preserves the additive fields without a history migration.',
		'Propagation includes all three provider mappings, pruning image estimates and recoverable markers, READ_BLOB records, shared live/restored transcript items and rebase payloads. Terminal frame grouping previously hid consecutive nonprompt images; only prompt image runs now merge. Web rows already retain every image card and reuse durable blob links. No Card edits, Chromium, paid benchmark calls, dependencies or new caches. Focused normal tests, tsc and changed-file lint pass; initial pruning helper-shadowing failure was fixed. Full verification outputs remain in private temporary logs.',
		'Review caught two recovery gaps: mapping refs with a throwing callback discarded surviving blobs, and multi-block user records serialized text without attaching images. READ_BLOB now collects image refs from the selected value or every user-record sibling, preserves the existing text serialization/page, and reports each failed read without dropping valid neighbors. Existing mixed-batch coverage deletes one stored source after initial recovery; a sibling-record case covers legacy, plural and direct images plus partial and total deletion.',
